        {
          "say": "Compare the complete contract with each registered lane. The fast public lane lacks several requirements. The public cited lane still fails the private-data boundary. Three private cited-review lanes satisfy the supplied checks, so these three enter the feasible set.\n",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 16.168,
          "duration": 15.768,
          "until": 16.817999999999998
        },
        {
          "say": "Inspect the cheap text lane. Its data flag and price look acceptable, but schema, citations, and review fail. Lower cost cannot repair those missing capabilities. The matrix keeps each failed field visible so an operator can explain the rejected route rather than guessing from a single Boolean.\n",
          "start": 16.817999999999998,
          "end": 35.226,
          "duration": 18.408,
          "until": 35.876
        },
        {
          "say": "Increase the private input beyond every registered capacity. Now no lane survives. The gateway returns an explicit escalation. Real dispatch must count each lane's actual serialized input and output reservation, then recheck current region, retention, credentials, and registry revision against the full application policy.\n",
